WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.700 --> 00:00:05.590
A charge request reaches your payment API.

2
00:00:05.590 --> 00:00:12.335
Before anything charges the card, it passes three checks: logging, auth, and an idempotency check.

3
00:00:12.533 --> 00:00:18.065
Each check either answers now, and the request goes no further, or hands it to the next one.

4
00:00:18.267 --> 00:00:21.038
This one has a token and the key 7781.

5
00:00:21.038 --> 00:00:24.903
Every check passes it on, and the charge answers 200.

6
00:00:24.903 --> 00:00:28.185
On the way back out, logging writes its line.

7
00:00:28.400 --> 00:00:29.779
Send it again.

8
00:00:29.779 --> 00:00:34.899
Idempotency has seen 7781, so it answers 409 itself.

9
00:00:35.133 --> 00:00:39.386
Key 7782 arrives with no token, and auth answers 401.

10
00:00:39.386 --> 00:00:44.683
The client adds the token and retries, and this time it's charged.

11
00:00:45.500 --> 00:00:50.392
That's a chain of responsibility: each link answers now, or calls the next.

12
00:00:50.600 --> 00:00:55.082
Now swap auth and idempotency, and replay the last two requests.

13
00:00:55.082 --> 00:00:57.182
What does the fixed retry get?

14
00:00:57.182 --> 00:00:58.023
Pause on it.

15
00:01:00.200 --> 00:01:00.558
409.

16
00:01:00.558 --> 00:01:10.127
Idempotency took key 7782 before auth turned that request away, so the honest retry looks like a duplicate.

17
00:01:10.127 --> 00:01:12.631
Order 7782 is never charged.

18
00:01:12.631 --> 00:01:15.672
The order of the list is behavior.

19
00:01:16.633 --> 00:01:19.157
State is the other half of this lesson.

20
00:01:19.157 --> 00:01:25.500
A payment goes from Created to Authorized, Captured and Refunded, and a Decline can fail it early.

21
00:01:25.700 --> 00:01:29.571
Each state accepts only some events, and picks the next state.

22
00:01:29.571 --> 00:01:32.255
Authorize moves this payment to Authorized.

23
00:01:32.255 --> 00:01:34.253
Capture moves it on to Captured.

24
00:01:34.433 --> 00:01:37.765
A new payment, still Created, gets a Capture.

25
00:01:37.765 --> 00:01:38.728
What happens?

26
00:01:38.728 --> 00:01:39.616
Pause on it.

27
00:01:41.800 --> 00:01:42.490
Rejected.

28
00:01:42.490 --> 00:01:46.933
Created has no rule for Capture, so the transition throws.

29
00:01:47.867 --> 00:01:51.857
In code, that's sealed states, sealed events, and one pure function.

30
00:01:51.857 --> 00:01:55.965
It switches on the state, then on the event, and anything else throws.

31
00:01:56.767 --> 00:02:05.861
The rule: a chain passes the request along until one link answers, and in a state machine, the current state decides what may happen next.

32
00:02:06.567 --> 00:02:07.603
A quick check.

33
00:02:07.603 --> 00:02:11.598
A Refund arrives for a payment that's only Authorized.

34
00:02:11.598 --> 00:02:12.560
What happens?

35
00:02:14.500 --> 00:02:15.295
Rejected.

36
00:02:15.295 --> 00:02:18.033
Only Captured accepts a Refund.
